WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:05.990
It is going to be a very, very ugly several
years for the Trump family.

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:13.250
Donald Trump's organization is under criminal
investigation now on the eve of Donald Trump

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:14.250
leaving office.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:21.000
And I expect that January 21st, twenty twenty
one, meaning Thursday is going to be a fascinating

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.370
day for Trump News.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:30.530
Trump is about to get whacked from three hundred
and sixty degrees with all sorts of investigations.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:35.920
CNN reporting that the Manhattan district
attorney's office is expanding its criminal.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:41.480
Yeah, this is a criminal investigation into
the Trump organization's finances.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:46.690
It will include the family compound in Westchester
County.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:53.430
Prosecutors are interested in this property
called Seven Springs because it is related

00:00:53.430 --> 00:01:00.210
to many possible financial crimes, including
understating by dramatic amounts the value

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:06.020
of properties to save on taxes while inflating
the value of those same properties when they're

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.810
used as collateral for loans.

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:10.969
We've covered that before this investigation.

00:01:10.969 --> 00:01:13.329
Again, it is a criminal investigation.

00:01:13.329 --> 00:01:18.709
It also is drawing closer not just to Trump
himself, but to Eric Trump, not exactly known

00:01:18.709 --> 00:01:20.549
as the smart one.

00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:24.479
Eric Trump is the executive vice president
of the Trump Organization.

00:01:24.479 --> 00:01:31.280
He was directly involved in the apparent riff
raff related to this property.

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:33.499
Subpoenas are going out.

00:01:33.499 --> 00:01:41.200
There are requests for all sorts of files,
emails, correspondence, and this really is

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.200
a threat to Trump.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.039
Now, I want to be clear.

00:01:44.039 --> 00:01:46.529
This is not likely to put Trump in prison.

00:01:46.529 --> 00:01:52.569
These are criminal investigations into the
organization, which would likely, if taken

00:01:52.569 --> 00:01:54.349
to their full conclusion.

00:01:54.349 --> 00:02:02.259
And if they find guilt, they would lead to
fines and potentially criminal charges against

00:02:02.259 --> 00:02:03.429
lower level people.

00:02:03.429 --> 00:02:06.069
Now, Eric Trump could count as a lower level
person here.

00:02:06.069 --> 00:02:10.399
I don't expect to see Eric Don Jr. or Ivanka
locked up, much like I don't expect to see

00:02:10.399 --> 00:02:11.399
Donald Trump locked up.

00:02:11.399 --> 00:02:13.540
We have to have reasonable expectations.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:17.010
But this is something that is going to grow
and grow and grow.

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:20.930
And remember that within 24 hours, Donald
Trump will no longer have the shield of the

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:24.549
presidency to delay lawsuits and investigations.

00:02:24.549 --> 00:02:27.870
One of the arguments that has been used by
Donald Trump's lawyers with some degree of

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:32.439
success for the last four years, even while
Trump was was the nominee, the Republican

00:02:32.439 --> 00:02:34.880
nominee back in 2016.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.879
One of the arguments that Trump lawyers have
used is this would encumber Donald Trump's

00:02:38.879 --> 00:02:42.180
ability to carry out his duties as president
of the United States.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.180
We have to put this off.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.180
We have to put this off.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.180
We have to put this off.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:49.579
But now, within 24 hours, that's no longer
going to be an argument.

00:02:49.579 --> 00:02:56.250
And we have both criminal and civil investigations
happening related to the Seven Springs property

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:00.379
and a whole bunch of other aspects of the
Trump organization.

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:05.230
We also are seeing the resumption of sexual
assault cases against Donald Trump.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:11.519
And while I maintain I do not believe we will
see a former U.S. president in prison any

00:03:11.519 --> 00:03:17.750
time soon, and that means up to and including
Donald Trump, this really could encumber Trump

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:19.140
for a very long time.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:24.230
I know there are some in my audience who think
Trump could end up in prison there awaiting

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:25.689
for the perp walk.

00:03:25.689 --> 00:03:27.220
I don't think we're going to see that.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:30.969
But the next couple of years are going to
be nuts regardless.

00:03:30.969 --> 00:03:36.480
Prepare yourselves to be unable to keep up
with the legal fiasco that is about to hit

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.300
Donald Trump's family.

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:39.300
It's I look.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:43.689
Forward to trying to keep up with it, but
it will be really difficult to keep up with

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:46.329
all that the Trump family is about to get
hit with.

00:03:46.329 --> 00:03:52.860
The biggest challenge right now facing prosecutors
is that there is so much possible criminal

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:57.810
behavior to investigate that it will take
years to unravel.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:03.989
They are going to have to break it up into
pieces and different offices, different squads,

00:04:03.989 --> 00:04:08.030
different investigative teams are going to
have to look at different elements of it.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:11.170
And remember, we still have money laundering
through the campaign.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:18.070
There are allegations that close to I believe
it was 160 or 170 million dollars was effectively

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:19.070
laundered.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:24.410
These were donations from Trump supporters
meant to go to the campaign.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:29.570
Hundreds of millions of dollars were reportedly
laundered through a company controlled by

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:36.040
Trump's former campaign manager, Brad Parr
scale, and used to be funneled back to Trump

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:41.560
family members and to shell corporations with
the doing of Jared Kushner.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:46.190
That story alone like that has nothing to
do with the Seven Springs property that has

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:50.550
nothing to do with lies told for tax benefits
by the Trump family.

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:52.660
It that's a separate story.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:57.490
The campaign money laundering story that one
alone could take two years to unravel.

00:04:57.490 --> 00:05:02.880
So regardless of what comes of it, this is
going to be hell for the Trump family for

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:03.880
years.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:06.420
The legal fees are going to explode.

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:09.280
Whether Trump will pay them is a question
that remains open.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:14.380
We already know that even though Rudy Giuliani
was building 20 grand a day for his work on

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:19.520
Trump's so-called election fraud campaign,
Trump has said don't pay Rudy.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:22.590
So who knows whether the lawyers will be paid?

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:26.970
But millions of dollars in legal fees will
be billed and it is going to be a wild couple

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:27.970
of years.

